</div> </div><br /> Marcus Verus and Dylan were the first to come to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T15:07:14-07:00","id":1481013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481008#post1481008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Marcus Verus and Dylan were the first to come to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Either of them is somewhat improbable considering that, unlike Vykos who is actually an Obertus Tzimisce and descendant of the Dracon, they are unconnected by blood to Antonius, being descended from the lines of Mithras and Tiamat respectively.<br /> <br /> What in Dylan's case could even mean he's a Baali forsworn by descent and (supposedly) doesn't even know it, since if there's a canon vampire to, alongside the likes of &quot;Huitzilopochtli&quot; or &quot;Baal-the-Destroyer&quot; (Ur-Shulgi), have been one of the many past holders of the title of Shaitan lost to Baali &amp; kindred history, Tiamat definitely fits the bill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-13-2022, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T16:27:49-07:00","id":1481022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481013#post1481013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Either of them is somewhat improbable considering that, unlike Vykos who is actually an Obertus Tzimisce and descendant of the Dracon, they are unconnected by blood to Antonius, being descended from the lines of Mithras and Tiamat respectively.<br /> <br /> What in Dylan's case could even mean he's a Baali forsworn by descent and (supposedly) doesn't even know it, since if there's a canon vampire to, alongside the likes of &quot;Huitzilopochtli&quot; or &quot;Baal-the-Destroyer&quot; (Ur-Shulgi), have been one of the many past holders of the title of Shaitan lost to Baali &amp; kindred history, Tiamat definitely fits the bill.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if we think in terms of Antonius the Gaul blood, it would be way harder to find a &quot;suitable&quot; successor as his line doesn't have many members listed, beyond those in Constantinople By Night. At least Dylan is mentioned as having been approached by Mariah, so it would be easier to imagine a connection, even though Dylan is WAAY weaker than the other two. Also, I don't see being Antonius descendant as a prerequisite to occupy his place in the triad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T16:49:04-07:00","id":1481025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481022#post1481022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, if we think in terms of Antonius the Gaul blood, it would be way harder to find a &quot;suitable&quot; successor as his line doesn't have many members listed, beyond those in Constantinople By Night. At least Dylan is mentioned as having been approached by Mariah, so it would be easier to imagine a connection, even though Dylan is WAAY weaker than the other two. Also, I don't see being Antonius descendant as a prerequisite to occupy his place in the triad.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It would go a long way toward a philosophical/spiritual connection, definitely much better than &quot;rando Ventrue i happened to meet a few months ago&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm extrapolating based on Vykos, that is definitely a blood descendant and may be seen as a philosophical/spiritual connection, not to mention the whole &quot;Dracon was phisically merged with me via Vicissitude for centuries, what i was dominated in forgetting&quot; angle too. Connections between Verus or Dylan to Antonius are tenuous at best, nill at most.<br /> <br /> Also, if Mary has to <i><b>seek out</b></i> a link/sucessor to Antonius, that is very much a storyline for a group of PCs to involve themselves and/or interfere with.<br /> Anyway, one may look into Antonius childer and their childer <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Antonius_(Constantinople)\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> (or in Constantinople by Night) for any potentially interesting NPCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> And that if one is trying to go for a &quot;clean&quot; replication of the Trinity, what is partly messed up by the fact Michael's &quot;extension&quot; is Mary, who is a Baali that diablerized him. Considering we have no info in how precisely Antonius was destroyed, it wouldn't be hard for a ST to insert some <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mahatma\" target=\"_blank\">unnamed individual who diablerized that ancient, or is the same under a disguise</a>.<br /> <br /> [Because to be fair, little to nothing in Mahatma's backstory and personality really fits with the fan theory of him being Byzar - a surviving Ectoris or Antonius under different name/title makes considerable more sense]<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what about Cappadocians? While Alexia Theusa was a pretty marked exception to this pattern, the clan's manias through medieval era fit with Michael's own degeneration into religious delusion to a Tee. Damn, except for the clan, the &quot;archangel&quot; might as well be Cappadocius under another guise!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-13-2022, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T17:39:24-07:00","id":1481030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481025#post1481025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It would go a long way toward a philosophical/spiritual connection, definitely much better than &quot;rando Ventrue i happened to meet a few months ago&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm extrapolating based on Vykos, that is definitely a blood descendant and may be seen as a philosophical/spiritual connection, not to mention the whole &quot;Dracon was phisically merged with me via Vicissitude for centuries, what i was dominated in forgetting&quot; angle too. Connections between Verus or Dylan to Antonius are tenuous at best, nill at most.<br /> <br /> Also, if Mary has to <i><b>seek out</b></i> a link/sucessor to Antonius, that is very much a storyline for a group of PCs to involve themselves and/or interfere with.<br /> Anyway, one may look into Antonius childer and their childer <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Antonius_(Constantinople)\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> (or in Constantinople by Night) for any potentially interesting NPCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> And that if one is trying to go for a &quot;clean&quot; replication of the Trinity, what is partly messed up by the fact Michael's &quot;extension&quot; is Mary, who is a Baali that diablerized him. Considering we have no info in how precisely Antonius was destroyed, it wouldn't be hard for a ST to insert some <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mahatma\" target=\"_blank\">unnamed individual who diablerized that ancient, or is the same under a disguise</a>.<br /> <br /> [Because to be fair, little to nothing in Mahatma's backstory and personality really fits with the fan theory of him being Byzar - a surviving Ectoris or Antonius under different name/title makes considerable more sense]<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what about Cappadocians? While Alexia Theusa was a pretty marked exception to this pattern, the clan's manias through medieval era fit with Michael's own degeneration into religious delusion to a Tee. Damn, except for the clan, the &quot;archangel&quot; might as well be Cappadocius under another guise!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the link about Antinious line, I had completely forgotten Belissarius was his child. In fact it's much better if the connection isn't &quot;random&quot;, so to speak. What you said makes more sense. But, in any case, wasn't Mahatma confirmed to be Byzar, that together with Lazarus and Japheth impersonates the Capuchin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T17:54:34-07:00","id":1481032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481030#post1481030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks for the link about Antinious line, I had completely forgotten Belissarius was his child. In fact it's much better if the connection isn't &quot;random&quot;, so to speak. What you said makes more sense. But, in any case, wasn't Mahatma confirmed to be Byzar, that together with Lazarus and Japheth impersonates the Capuchin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but remember not a few of the V20/V5 writers are fans like you and me uplifted to the writer chair. We all can let our pet theories/fanon get the best of us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Honestly, i find the confirmation questionable to say the least. But anyway.<br /> <br /> - Byzar could have returned on his own and then joined the other two.<br /> - The Capuchin could be a master of Auspex and Obfuscate acting in multiple fronts through a combination of disguises, illusion and discipline-enhanced psychic projection.<br /> - Japheth is supposed to have been <i>diablerized</i> by Claudius Giovanni. People usually don't return from that except <i>maybe </i>in the diablerist body (that said Augustus might have given Claudius carcass to the Capuchin as punishment to the former and reward to the latter. Hmmmmm).<br /> <br /> Among a bunch of other possible explanations for the &quot;trio of Cappadocian methuselahs&quot; info on the Capuchin's identity, that could be as true or false as one wants it to be.<br /> <br /> [In my own games the Capuchin is &quot;just&quot; Constancia, who happened to change sides among other things because she was Ambrogino's sire - and far more involved with the Giovanni than many other recognized - a long time before Augustus' act of usurpation]<br /> <br /> <br /> But seriously, read Mahatma's history, <b>only</b> thing in common between him and Byzar is &quot;existed in Constantinople a long time ago&quot; and being 4th gen (that in Mahatma's case could be the product of diablerie, he <b><i>definitely </i></b>had the temper for such a thing in his years before meeting Saulot, might be said).<br /> <br /> The WW wiki itself points out there are some pretty glaring contradictions. The part where Alexia is cited as founder pretty blatantly spells it out that Mahatma is <b>not</b> Byzantium's real kindred &quot;founder&quot;.<br /> <br /> We don't even know Mahatma's actual clan is and based on discipline spread he could be Salubri, Ventrue and other things besides just as well if not better than Cappadocian. As an aside, Mahatma's sire is named as Laodice - that happens to be defnitely a greek <i>female </i>name, unlike Cappadocius whom, afaik, has always been described as a male antediluvian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-13-2022, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T21:45:53-07:00","id":1481045,"title":"","content":"BJD describes Michael as looking for a vampire who has died and been resurrected, as he and the Dracon have, for their third.<br /> <br /> I like Mithras for the role, after he's finished emerging from within Monty Coven.<br /> <br /> When I posted my first response to this thread, I wasn't aware that you were setting your game in the 16th Century. The status quo of each of these characters is liable to be very different, unless you're actively playing around with the timeline for your story. The revelation of Michael's survival of his diablerie and the rebirth of the Dracon from the body of Vykos are both relatively recent modern events in the published timeline, both taking place after the end of the original line of books in 2004. Mary might very well just be wandering the Earth and jabbering to herself as the ancient within her begins to wake, or she may have full control and just be doing her routine Baali/Decani scheming in this era. Again, it's really about whatever works best for your story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-14-2022, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T09:15:13-07:00","id":1481075,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11599\" data-vbnamecard=\"11599\">Reasor</a> I can't see Mithras joining the Trinity as he dislikes Christainity in general and sees himself as a God and wouldn't play well with Dracon and Michael/Mari.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T09:40:46-07:00","id":1481083,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> I agree that it doesn't need to be a Ventrue or some distant member of his line to fill in Antinous role in the Trinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T13:07:32-07:00","id":1481110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1480969#post1480969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wouldn't know either way. Where is that one cited out of curiosity?</div> </div> </div> </div>BECKETT\u2019S JYHAD DIARY, p. 451","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","name":"trueann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T14:40:11-07:00","id":1481128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We don't even know Mahatma's actual clan is and based on discipline spread he could be Salubri, Ventrue and other things besides just as well if not better than Cappadocian. As an aside, Mahatma's sire is named as Laodice - that happens to be defnitely a greek <i>female </i>name, unlike Cappadocius whom, afaik, has always been described as a male antediluvian. </div> </div> </div>In fact before WW saying Mahatma was Byzar, I used to think he was most likely a Salubri.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I posted my first response to this thread, I wasn't aware that you were setting your game in the 16th Century. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the fact that it's in the 16th century changes a lot of things, but I'd be willing to adapt dates to fit my story, it's like the least of my problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't see Mithras joining the Trinity as he dislikes Christainity in general and sees himself as a God and wouldn't play well with Dracon and Michael/Mari. </div> </div> </div>I also don't see Mithras willing to share power in a trinity and, even more importantly, to be a part of a &quot;christian thing&quot;, even in a heretical way as the <i>Triumvirate.</i> stands Mithras is the god of war and the sun, he never liked Christianism. That's why I thought about Marcus Verus, as it's sometimes implied that he somehow grew dissatisfied with his sire and thus could change allegiances, like Cretheus did before him. Still, I'd prefer to choose someone more interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree that it doesn't need to be a Ventrue or some distant member of his line to fill in Antinous role in the Trinity. </div> </div> </div>Yes, especially seeing that Antonius was basically betrayed by the other two, I don't see a strong reason as to why the cainite needs to be a Ventrue and much less from Antonius' line.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer the third member was a Ventrue, like Antonius, but I'm still to find a good candidate. Dylan is interesting, but far too weak for the role...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T16:15:06-07:00","id":1481143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trueann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481110#post1481110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BECKETT\u2019S JYHAD DIARY, p. 451</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks a lot. Just checked, literal one line reference - in meta/hook format to boot - and nothing else.<br /> <br /> Feeling it's another Mahatma = Byzar NPC conflation hiccup, this time with the Lair of the Hidden <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Council_of_Twelve\" target=\"_blank\">Inconnu-Infernalist cabal</a>, growing.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-15-2022, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T12:09:58-07:00","id":1481189,"title":"","content":"-<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481128#post1481128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact before WW saying Mahatma was Byzar, I used to think he was most likely a Salubri.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, the fact that it's in the 16th century changes a lot of things, but I'd be willing to adapt dates to fit my story, it's like the least of my problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, especially seeing that Antonius was basically betrayed by the other two, I don't see a strong reason as to why the cainite needs to be a Ventrue and much less from Antonius' line.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer the third member was a Ventrue, like Antonius, but I'm still to find a good candidate. Dylan is interesting, but far too weak for the role...</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Dylan is a few centuries out of place, considering he was embraced in WWII during the Blitz. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Going back to Antonius, the best options i see are either &quot;Antonius never died, he became Mahatma&quot; and trying to convert him when he feels betrayed and the need to let his past go for the sake of enlightnement/Golconda both as a source of conflict... Or <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Caius\" target=\"_blank\">this guy</a>, because.<br /> <br /> - Childe of Antonius the Gaul? Check.<br /> - Possessed of an unhealthy obsession with Michael (who spurned him)? Check.<br /> - The oldest and most powerful Ventrue, or kindred in Constantinople beside Michael, with the possible exceptions of Petronius and Alexia Theusa? Check (though his given stats do not reflect this, Marcus Verrus' original DA:V were also quite underwhelming)<br /> - Incredibly vague ending that might have involved an encounter with Mary just after she consumed Michael? Check, so much, so bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> Seriously, if there's someone to survive a fight with freshly empowered Mary, spend centuries hunting her down for the sake of revenge and then, after finding out about Michael's flagging soul fragment, to do a crazy swerve in attempting to boost that spark within Mary back into unlife, in a demented ploy to finally be together with his beloved, Caius is <b>totally</b> the person to be that kind of complete nutcase of a gothic $#itshow.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would like to point out that, while i have focused in the idea of a still unliving Antonius or members of his brood in my picks, that has been more &quot;get those canon characters with personal stakes in the subject&quot; perspective. It just happens that in Constantinople by Night many times both things go together.<br /> <br /> But when it comes to crossing (and blurring) the lines between heaven and hell, there is at least <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Khay&#39;tall\" target=\"_blank\">one strong candidate </a>that comes to mind while being no blood relation of the Trinity kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-15-2022, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T14:28:08-07:00","id":1481201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Dylan is a few centuries out of place, considering he was embraced in WWII during the Blitz. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Surely, cannon Dylan is at least 4 centuries out of place, lol. I mentioned him, because I have another version of him I made for a dark ages setting, some 4 years ago, but still it would be far from optimal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Childe of Antonius the Gaul? Check.<br /> - Possessed of an unhealthy obsession with Michael (who spurned him)? Check.<br /> - The oldest and most powerful Ventrue, or kindred in Constantinople beside Michael, with the possible exceptions of Petronius and Alexia Theusa? Check (though his given stats do not reflect this, Marcus Verrus' original DA:V were also quite underwhelming)<br /> - Incredibly vague ending that might have involved an encounter with Mary just after she consumed Michael? Check, so much, so bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> Seriously, if there's someone to survive a fight with freshly empowered Mary, spend centuries hunting her down for the sake of revenge and then, after finding out about Michael's flagging soul fragment, to do a crazy swerve in attempting to boost that spark within Mary back into unlife, in a demented ploy to finally be together with his beloved, Caius is <b>totally</b> the person to be that kind of complete nutcase of a gothic $#itshow. </div> </div> </div>Yes, by changing the story a bit (By the way, his destruction always felt a bit too &quot;weird&quot; or &quot;convenient&quot; to me, so to speak), Caius is a great candidate indeed. I would add that I agree that his given stats are terribly underwhelming (as were the original for Marcus Verus, as you mentioned, V20 kind of fixed it, though), so underwhelming it almost sound as if it was made on purpose lol, but that's very easy to fix. I think he possesses the qualities to fill the role and as obsessed as he was about Michael, he is certainly better than the other alternatives at least. <br /> <br /> I think making Antonius survive would be perhaps too convenient and Khay'tal feels a bit out of place for the role, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> My intention in making this new Triumvirate is more to blur the line between heaven and hell, not exactly to make Triumvirate 2.0, but as it stands, Caius seems the best candidate to fill the role of his sire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T20:26:06-07:00","id":1481209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481201#post1481201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Surely, cannon Dylan is at least 4 centuries out of place, lol. I mentioned him, because I have another version of him I made for a dark ages setting, some 4 years ago, but still it would be far from optimal.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, plenty of wars in the late middle ages and renaissance for one to fit a &quot;dark ages equivalent&quot; into. But yeah, Dylan is not a great fit anyway, his whole reason to be cited in the first place is being the recurrent infernalist in BJD's plotline, truth be told. By that logic any other major infernalist NPC might do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481201#post1481201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, by changing the story a bit (By the way, his destruction always felt a bit too &quot;weird&quot; or &quot;convenient&quot; to me, so to speak), Caius is a great candidate indeed. I would add that I agree that his given stats are terribly underwhelming (as were the original for Marcus Verus, as you mentioned, V20 kind of fixed it, though), so underwhelming it almost sound as if it was made on purpose lol, but that's very easy to fix. I think he possesses the qualities to fill the role and as obsessed as he was about Michael, he is certainly better than the other alternatives at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously the writer was much more of a Belisarius fanboy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, here goes a quick sketch of a fixed sheet for something of a springboard:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Caius, Basileus of the Antonian Ventrue<br /> Clan: Ventrue<br /> Sire: Antonius<br /> Nature: Penitent<br /> Demeanor: Autocrat<br /> Generation: 5th<br /> Embrace: 325 CE<br /> Apparent age: Mid-40s<br /> <br /> physical: Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> social: Charisma 6, Manipulation 3, Appearance 3<br /> mental: Perception 6, Intelligence 4, Wits 4<br /> <br /> talents: Alertness 4, Brawl 4, Dodge 3, Empathy 1, Intimidation 4, Leadership 4, Subterfuge 6<br /> skills: Animal Ken 1, Archery 3, Crafts (Weapons) 3, Etiquette 4, Melee 5, Ride 4, Stealth 4, Survival 3<br /> knowledges: Academics 3, Hearth Wisdom 3, Investigation 1, Law 4, Linguistics 3, Politics 5, Seneschal 4<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Auspex 4, Celerity 3, Dominate 7, Fortitude 6, Obfuscate 1, Potence 6, Presence 4<br /> <br /> backgrounds: Allies 3 (Alexia Theusa), Contacts 5, Herd 5, Influence 5, Retainers 5, Status 6<br /> virtues: Conscience 3, Self-Control 3, Courage 5<br /> morality: Humanity 6<br /> willpower: 7 </div> </div> </div>Did some comparison to Belisarius for reference, tweaked a dot or two after looking into Alexia. More of a quick-&amp;-dirty starting point than anything definite.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481201#post1481201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think making Antonius survive would be perhaps too convenient</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? I dare say it's his final death that is too convenient, 4th gens don't usually get neatly destroyed by decree, even if the one calling the Wild Hunt is another 4th gen....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481201#post1481201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and Khay'tal feels a bit out of place for the role, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> My intention in making this new Triumvirate is more to blur the line between heaven and hell, not exactly to make Triumvirate 2.0, but as it stands, Caius seems the best candidate to fill the role of his sire.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, Khay'tal might not fit any particular element of the Trinity, but as &quot;snake in paradise&quot; of the Dream, the crucible of virtue tempered in the fires of temptation, i'd say he would be quite appropriate a character to involve itself in any kind of twisted return of Michael's work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-15-2023, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T22:08:03-07:00","id":1481213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously the writer was much more of a Belisarius fanboy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Yes, perhaps he was too inspired by the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belisarius\" target=\"_blank\">historical figur</a>e, hahaha... <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> his whole reason to be cited in the first place is being the recurrent infernalist in BJD's plotline, truth be told. </div> </div> </div>I also somehow think he's very hot (please don't judge me), lol! So that's another reason, but still he is basically discarded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, here goes a quick sketch of a fixed sheet for something of a springboard: </div> </div> </div>It's certainly much better than the original, I'd say I'd raise his Manipulation a bit, give him some Occultism and perhaps raise his Presence to 5, but it's MUCH BETTER as it is than the original from Constantinople By Night, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it? I dare say it's his final death that is too convenient, 4th gens don't usually get neatly destroyed by decree, even if the one calling the Wild Hunt is another 4th gen.... </div> </div> </div>From one perspective it is in fact too convenient (but still not as much as Hardestadt being killed by a single shotgun shot from Theo Bell or Jalan Aajav dying in a plane crash or even Karsh being defeated by Xaviar and Theo Bell LOL), at the same time though, it's one of the main points in the original story from CbN. Antonius destruction acted as a catalyst for the destruction of the Dream, by making the guilty Dracon leave the city and Michael to fall deeper in his delusions of divinity. So, all in all, convenient or not it has great significance to the story, as the story would be completely different in the absence of this fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True, Khay'tal might not fit any particular element of the Trinity, but as &quot;snake in paradise&quot; of the Dream, the crucible of virtue tempered in the fires of temptation, i'd say he would be quite appropriate a character to involve itself in any kind of twisted return of Michael's work. </div> </div> </div>Aye, the &quot;snake in paradise&quot; has its importance, as does Dimities, by the way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T07:12:00-07:00","id":1481235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481213#post1481213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, perhaps he was too inspired by the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belisarius\" target=\"_blank\">historical figur</a>e, hahaha...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he <b>is</b> considered one of history's greatest generals, so justified.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481213#post1481213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also somehow think he's very hot (please don't judge me), lol! So that's another reason, but still he is basically discarded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, no kinkshaming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481213#post1481213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's certainly much better than the original, I'd say I'd raise his Manipulation a bit, give him some Occultism and perhaps raise his Presence to 5, but it's MUCH BETTER as it is than the original from Constantinople By Night, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the point was balancing him a bit with the other stated out 5th gens in the book (though i did forget to check <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gesu\" target=\"_blank\">Gesu</a>, bummer) than anything really finished, go for whatever you prefer.<br /> <br /> That said, i <b>do</b> like the idea of misguided &quot;mystics&quot; and cult leaders that are far more grounded in a combination of theology, philosophy, folk wisdom, sheer power of personality than any real understanding of the kind of esoteric forces they might end up dealing with. Michael's own cult is powered by oodles of that, truth be told. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> [Yes, Michael has awesome levels of Hearth wisdom &amp; Occult both. Gesu, of similar influence in his own branches of the church and cults, not so much]<br /> <br /> Also really reccomend <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Name_of_the_Rose\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, for a great reference into deep dives into the philosophic, spiritual &amp; theological with little to no whiff of the occult/supernatural to the drama and disputes involved.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481213#post1481213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From one perspective it is in fact too convenient (but still not as much as Hardestadt being killed by a single shotgun shot from Theo Bell or Jalan Aajav dying in a plane crash or even Karsh being defeated by Xaviar and Theo Bell LOL),</div> </div> </div> </div>Hardestadt is an overated blowhard. Also, Dragonsbreath rounds with Ward against Vampires, never leave the coffin without them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (And well, a plane crash <b>could </b>be quite problematic even for Jalan Aajav if it happened during daylight hours - him actually doing a long flight where he might be vulnerable to that, now that's another story....)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481213#post1481213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">at the same time though, it's one of the main points in the original story from CbN. Antonius destruction acted as a catalyst for the destruction of the Dream, by making the guilty Dracon leave the city and Michael to fall deeper in his delusions of divinity. So, all in all, convenient or not it has great significance to the story, as the story would be completely different in the absence of this fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too true that, the whole &quot;lost love&quot; and general malaise dynamic resulting from Antonius' destruction runs counter to Mahatma's continuous passive-agressive manipulations and shenanigans against the byzantines.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481213#post1481213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aye, the &quot;snake in paradise&quot; has its importance, as does Dimities, by the way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, Dimities. either of them can add much to the equation, both, either at cross purposes or working together.... oh boy.<br /> <br /> As an aside, DA's portrayal of the Inconnu is just utterly ridiculous - in CbN it's fine and acceptable because we learn of them through Dimities, so everything could be an elaborate morass of conspiratory demented nonsense that exists only in his broken mind and soul.<br /> <br /> But trying to take that at face value, as other writers seem to do in later books, that's patently absurd as that particular take fits with nothing before and after, the group has a whole different focus - it sounds much more like some cabal or faction of the Tal'Mahe'Ra/Manus Nigrum than anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> [Not to mention <i>Inconnu </i>comes from french, <b>not </b>latin, what the hell were those people smoking...]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-15-2023, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T12:57:14-07:00","id":1481255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, the point was balancing him a bit with the other stated out 5th gens in the book (though i did forget to check <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gesu\" target=\"_blank\">Gesu</a>, bummer) than anything really finished, go for whatever you prefer. </div> </div> </div>Something that needs to be mentioned, though, is the fact that the perceived level of kindred power varies A LOT depending on the book you read, but as you mentioned, Gesu is much younger than Caius, but still has much better traits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But trying to take that at face value, as other writers seem to do in later books, that's patently absurd as that particular take fits with nothing before and after, the group has a whole different focus - it sounds much more like some cabal or faction of the Tal'Mahe'Ra/Manus Nigrum than anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> [Not to mention <i>Inconnu </i>comes from french, <b>not </b>latin, what the hell were those people smoking...] </div> </div> </div>This is so true, I never liked how the Inconnu was portrayed in CbN (nor could I understand why such an elder sect from Rome would have a French name for the matter...lol). In some of the chronicles I ran I made the so called Inconnu one of the arms of the Manus Nigrum/Tal'Mahe'Ra, so that it would make more sense. I still think it would make them much more coherent and interesting. While we could say only the Twelve were converted through Saulot and then abandoned their old allegiances to form a new cult, so to speak, dedicated to finding Golconda (and killing Methuselah around the world from the safety of their castle that is protected by an earthbound demon lol). I think it definitely works better this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T16:28:05-07:00","id":1481269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481255#post1481255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something that needs to be mentioned, though, is the fact that the perceived level of kindred power varies A LOT depending on the book you read, but as you mentioned, Gesu is much younger than Caius, but still has much better traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it can vary sometimes wildly even within the same book, between different books much more so.<br /> That said, i kind of give Gesu a pass in that he's clearly meant to be a special snowflake prodigy kind of figure.<br /> Possibly a kind of &quot;accursed chosen one&quot; if the matter of the Eldest's warning serves as indicator.<br /> <br /> As an aside i can perfectly see him surviving and relocating his cult within the russian orthodox church or any of the many european countries influenced by byzantine culture, what could make him into another potential factor to account for into this drama.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481255#post1481255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is so true, I never liked how the Inconnu was portrayed in CbN (nor could I understand why such an elder sect from Rome would have a French name for the matter...lol). In some of the chronicles I ran I made the so called Inconnu one of the arms of the Manus Nigrum/Tal'Mahe'Ra, so that it would make more sense. I still think it would make them much more coherent and interesting. While we could say only the Twelve were converted through Saulot and then abandoned their old allegiances to form a new cult, so to speak, dedicated to finding Golconda (and killing Methuselah around the world from the safety of their castle that is protected by an earthbound demon lol). I think it definitely works better this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It all depends on one's game to be fair. A group of roman remnants could play out similar or quite differently from the Manus Nigrum/Tal'Mahe'Ra, Amici Noctis and other kindred secret societies depending on what elements one wants to focus on and become an interesting antagonist (or patron) on its own.<br /> <br /> What galls at me is some writer trying to tack on such an idea into an already existing faction - and one that makes no flipping sense whatsoever to connect in such a way, for that matter. Anyway, Gregorius forsaking them and going on its own or still being a part of the group (even if a somewhat resentful one) can affect one's game in some quite different ways.<br /> <br /> All of that said, in the context of CobN the &quot;roman Inconnu&quot; is quite simple an issue to deal with, as Dimities is the only hook to that idea in the whole book, meaning a ST could decide, if he has no interest in the idea of a &quot;ugly secret past of the Inconnu&quot; (that makes no sense whatsoever) the sect as described there exists only within his painfully fractured mind.<br /> <br /> [What can be scary aplenty on its own, as even by the book he has Auspex 4, Dementation 6, Dominate 3, Obfuscate 3, Presence 3 - he could pretty much fabricate hyper-complex split personalities representing his &quot;mentors&quot; from a mix of delirium, facts gathered from visions, gleaned thoughts and more (cobweb, *cough*, *cough*), and then &quot;upload&quot; those personas into any kindred 6th gen or weaker as their personalities, diablerie ghosts or whatever one wants them to believe]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-16-2022, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T17:09:53-07:00","id":1481270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, i kind of give Gesu a pass in that he's clearly meant to be a special snowflake prodigy kind of figure.<br /> Possibly a kind of &quot;accursed chosen one&quot; if the matter of the Eldest's warning serves as indicator. </div> </div> </div>In fact, I would go as far as buff his traits to be honest. My main problem is the fact that the others are balanced somewhat poorly in the book and between &quot;too weak&quot; or &quot;too strong&quot; I almost always opt for the latter. I'm very used to the idea of crossovers, since I started storytelling (many years in the past hahaha...), so I've never been fond of the idea of having an important Cainite character being killed with a single werewolf or mage attack lol, so this &quot;upbringing&quot; kind of explains my preferences, so to speak. You see, Melinda Galbraith is younger than Caius, but look at the huge difference between their traits! Between these choices, I would almost always opt for Melinda's approach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It all depends on one's game to be fair. A group of roman remnants could play out similar or quite differently from the Manus Nigrum/Tal'Mahe'Ra, Amici Noctis and other kindred secret societies depending on what elements one wants to focus on and become an interesting antagonist (or patron) on its own. </div> </div> </div>Most certainly, it depends on the game/story. I don't see a problem with the idea of Roman kindreds like this one incarnation of the Inconnu, I was joking more because of consistency and the fact that Inconnu (being a French name) isn't perhaps the best choice of name for an old Roman cainite's secret society. But the &quot;secret kindred society&quot; one is going to use in a chronicle can vary a lot on what the story needs, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-17T07:53:53-07:00","id":1481289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481270#post1481270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact, I would go as far as buff his traits to be honest. My main problem is the fact that the others are balanced somewhat poorly in the book and between &quot;too weak&quot; or &quot;too strong&quot; I almost always opt for the latter. I'm very used to the idea of crossovers, since I started storytelling (many years in the past hahaha...), so I've never been fond of the idea of having an important Cainite character being killed with a single werewolf or mage attack lol, so this &quot;upbringing&quot; kind of explains my preferences, so to speak. You see, Melinda Galbraith is younger than Caius, but look at the huge difference between their traits! Between these choices, I would almost always opt for Melinda's approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Gesu's stats are quite fine imho for the period CoBN and Bitter Crusade are set at, between 1194-1230, quite respectable for a 500 year old kindred. It's just that:<br /> <br /> - He's clearly not a methuselah, that is what most people kind of expect when they see &quot;5th generation&quot; in a sheet.<br /> - <i>Definitely </i><b>not </b>made with combat in mind.<br /> <br /> But he's good - someone with the same numbers swapped into a different build could be quite the combat monster among other things.<br /> <br /> <br /> About Galbraith, well, she's a Masquerade NPC (from Chaos Factor that is notoriously gonzo, to boot), VtDA/DA:V NPCs were clearly made with a different scale in mind, possibly in part to make less of overpowering threats for neonate PCs.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Children_of_the_Night\" target=\"_blank\">Children of Night</a> has some character creation guidelines that while not perfect can work as a basis to adjust and tweak them that is mostly effective across multiple editions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481270#post1481270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most certainly, it depends on the game/story. I don't see a problem with the idea of Roman kindreds like this one incarnation of the Inconnu, I was joking more because of consistency and the fact that Inconnu (being a French name) isn't perhaps the best choice of name for an old Roman cainite's secret society. But the &quot;secret kindred society&quot; one is going to use in a chronicle can vary a lot on what the story needs, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>More importantly, do you think of using Dimities in your game and if so, how much of a role would &quot;the romans&quot; (kind of temped to call them <a href=\"https://hellsing.fandom.com/wiki/Incognito\" target=\"_blank\">Incognito</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) have or not in the drama of the return of the Trinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-17-2022, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-17T11:19:56-07:00","id":1481305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, Gesu's stats are quite fine imho for the period CoBN and Bitter Crusade are set at, between 1194-1230, quite respectable for a 500 year old kindred. It's just that: </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say they're bad, but for me his stats are just decent, not perfect, but still the thought that an important 5th generation kindred can be easily killed with a single attack gives me anxiety attacks lol<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - He's clearly not a methuselah, that is what most people kind of expect when they see &quot;5th generation&quot; in a sheet. </div> </div> </div>Certainly this influences the observer a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> VtDA/DA:V NPCs were clearly made with a different scale in mind, possibly in part to make less of overpowering threats for neonate PCs. </div> </div> </div>Well, I would most likely disagree on principle, Dark Ages is usually a much more threatening and combat heavy setting than the modern age. The thing is that the level of power of cainites varies WILDLY between different books, even when talking about the same period, like Dark Ages. Dark Ages France, for instance, have characters that would put even Galbraith to shame. Also, Chaos Factor is a crossover, usually books with that in mind have more powerful characters (Although the aforementioned Dark Ages France doesn't fit this description, but it's usually the case, e.g. Chaos Factor, Dark Alliance Vancouver, Rage Across Russia, etc). What gives me anxiety attacks in his character sheet is mainly because he hasn't a single dot in Fortitude (unlike his brother Symeon), i.e. he can be easily destroyed with a single attack. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More importantly, do you think of using Dimities in your game and if so, how much of a role would &quot;the romans&quot; (kind of temped to call them <a href=\"https://hellsing.fandom.com/wiki/Incognito\" target=\"_blank\">Incognito</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) have or not in the drama of the return of the Trinity. </div> </div> </div>Incognito is absolutely more fitting than Inconnu lol. Well, I still need to decide, but if I really use him, I'd probably make him a spy and &quot;agent of chaos&quot; working for a secret society with the aim of undermining the Triumvirate power by attempting to plunge Michael/Mariah deeper in his/her own insanity. That's why I mentioned the Manus Nigrum before, as it's one of their goals, to weaken and sow chaos in cainite society in order to undermine their power, also the Triumvirate would fit perfectly in the Tal'Mahe'Ra idea of &quot;cainite abuse&quot; that they say they fight against. But I stll need to think a lot about it, as with the Triunvirate reformed and &quot;in order&quot;, there would be fewer avenues to cainites like Khay'tal or Dimities to influence Michael.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T11:51:08-07:00","id":1481384,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Baaldam;n1481209]<br /> <br /> True, plenty of wars in the late middle ages and renaissance for one to fit a &quot;dark ages equivalent&quot; into. But yeah, Dylan is not a great fit anyway, his whole reason to be cited in the first place is being the recurrent infernalist in BJD's plotline, truth be told. By that logic any other major infernalist NPC might do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481201#post1481201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, by changing the story a bit (By the way, his destruction always felt a bit too &quot;weird&quot; or &quot;convenient&quot; to me, so to speak), Caius is a great candidate indeed. I would add that I agree that his given stats are terribly underwhelming (as were the original for Marcus Verus, as you mentioned, V20 kind of fixed it, though), so underwhelming it almost sound as if it was made on purpose lol, but that's very easy to fix. I think he possesses the qualities to fill the role and as obsessed as he was about Michael, he is certainly better than the other alternatives at least.<br /> <br /> Obviously the writer was much more of a Belisarius fanboy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, here goes a quick sketch of a fixed sheet for something of a springboard:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Did some comparison to Belisarius for reference, tweaked a dot or two after looking into Alexia. More of a quick-&amp;-dirty starting point than anything definite.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> Is it? I dare say it's his final death that is too convenient, 4th gens don't usually get neatly destroyed by decree, even if the one calling the Wild Hunt is another 4th gen....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> True, Khay'tal might not fit any particular element of the Trinity, but as &quot;snake in paradise&quot; of the Dream, the crucible of virtue tempered in the fires of temptation, i'd say he would be quite appropriate a character to involve itself in any kind of twisted return of Michael's work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't Khayt'al diablerized his childe a scant few decades after the 4th crusade for messing up so badly and weakening their clan's standing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T12:00:53-07:00","id":1481387,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Lysander;n1481384]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481209#post1481209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, plenty of wars in the late middle ages and renaissance for one to fit a &quot;dark ages equivalent&quot; into. But yeah, Dylan is not a great fit anyway, his whole reason to be cited in the first place is being the recurrent infernalist in BJD's plotline, truth be told. By that logic any other major infernalist NPC might do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wasn't Khayt'al diablerized his childe a scant few decades after the 4th crusade for messing up so badly and weakening their clan's standing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is it in the Dark Ages Setite Novel? Unfortunately I didn't read the DA Setite novel, I couldn't bring myself to care about the protagonist, so if it's there it explains what you said, as I don't remember reading about his destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T12:02:53-07:00","id":1481389,"title":"","content":"I remember reading it in Khayt'al write up in Constaninople By Night. In the destiny section, it mentions that he is betrayed by his childe and got consumed for his mistakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T13:43:46-07:00","id":1481398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481389#post1481389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading it in Khayt'al write up in Constaninople By Night. In the destiny section, it mentions that he is betrayed by his childe and got consumed for his mistakes.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IBnNe7zcv4WzRTRUPtRDMTvuGCChpL9X/view?usp=sharing\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> True, just saw <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IBnNe7zcv4WzRTRUPtRDMTvuGCChpL9X/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> on the book, for some reason I didn't remember it, I've never been a fan of the character tbh, but it's funny that while he wanted to influence Michael, he ended up being the one influenced by the Methuselah...<br /> <br /> PS: For some reason I couldn't upload the photo from my computer and had to use a link, is there an explanation for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 05-18-2022, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T23:27:26-07:00","id":1481427,"title":"","content":"While true, during the sacking of Constantinople in 1204, Khay'tall was ambushed by his favorite childe, Sarrasine, who drained his corporeal form of all its vitae in an attempt of diablerie.<br /> But Khay'tall, who expected something like that, had his own heart previously removed via Serpentis and placed in a scarab amulet created by Gregorius Lakeritos.<br /> The amulet eventually came into the possession of the Setite Andreas Aegyptus/Ankhesenaten (&quot;He-Who-Lives-For-The-Sun-God&quot;... what a strange name for a Settite...) who delivered the amulet to the Red Temple of Thebes.<br /> Okay, most of his clan regarded him as a heretic, thats true, but nothing further was described, and by the Revised Clanbook, tho' was a Founding Temple, the Red Temple, located in Thebes within modern Luxor, now largely deserted...<br /> Who knows, that amulet and the essence of Khay&quot;tall potentially could be still there or &quot;survived&quot; to the modern day<br /> And given Michael fondnes of that Snake, its not out of the realm of possibility, he would eventually try to find it to &quot;resurrect&quot; the Snake of the Garden<br /> Actually, both Michael and Mary would have a good reason; Mihael the same reason he had in the first place when accepted him in his city, and Mary for the exact reason he did with that opportunity, dragging down the Dream to Hell...<br /> Anyhow would be a really neat little story idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-19-2022, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T00:21:20-07:00","id":1481429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481427#post1481427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While true, during the sacking of Constantinople in 1204, Khay'tall was ambushed by his favorite childe, Sarrasine, who drained his corporeal form of all its vitae in an attempt of diablerie.<br /> But Khay'tall, who expected something like that, had his own heart previously removed via Serpentis and placed in a scarab amulet created by Gregorius Lakeritos.<br /> The amulet eventually came into the possession of the Setite Andreas Aegyptus/Ankhesenaten (&quot;He-Who-Lives-For-The-Sun-God&quot;... what a strange name for a Settite...) who delivered the amulet to the Red Temple of Thebes.<br /> Okay, most of his clan regarded him as a heretic, thats true, but nothing further was described, and by the Revised Clanbook, tho' was a Founding Temple, the Red Temple, located in Thebes within modern Luxor, now largely deserted...<br /> Who knows, that amulet and the essence of Khay&quot;tall potentially could be still there or &quot;survived&quot; to the modern day<br /> And given Michael fondnes of that Snake, its not out of the realm of possibility, he would eventually try to find it to &quot;resurrect&quot; the Snake of the Garden<br /> Actually, both Michael and Mary would have a good reason; Mihael the same reason he had in the first place when accepted him in his city, and Mary for the exact reason he did with that opportunity, dragging down the Dream to Hell...<br /> Anyhow would be a really neat little story idea</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now that you mentioned, you made it look more interesting. Perhaps I can find a use for him, that looks like a very interesting idea,I love this kind of story that defy people's normal assumptions of cainites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T01:21:27-07:00","id":1481433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481427#post1481427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While true, during the sacking of Constantinople in 1204, Khay'tall was ambushed by his favorite childe, Sarrasine, who drained his corporeal form of all its vitae in an attempt of diablerie.<br /> But Khay'tall, who expected something like that, had his own heart previously removed via Serpentis and placed in a scarab amulet created by Gregorius Lakeritos.<br /> The amulet eventually came into the possession of the Setite Andreas Aegyptus/Ankhesenaten (&quot;He-Who-Lives-For-The-Sun-God&quot;... what a strange name for a Settite...) who delivered the amulet to the Red Temple of Thebes.<br /> Okay, most of his clan regarded him as a heretic, thats true, but nothing further was described, and by the Revised Clanbook, tho' was a Founding Temple, the Red Temple, located in Thebes within modern Luxor, now largely deserted...<br /> Who knows, that amulet and the essence of Khay&quot;tall potentially could be still there or &quot;survived&quot; to the modern day<br /> And given Michael fondnes of that Snake, its not out of the realm of possibility, he would eventually try to find it to &quot;resurrect&quot; the Snake of the Garden<br /> Actually, both Michael and Mary would have a good reason; Mihael the same reason he had in the first place when accepted him in his city, and Mary for the exact reason he did with that opportunity, dragging down the Dream to Hell...<br /> Anyhow would be a really neat little story idea</div> </div> </div> </div>I had not thought of Khay'tall, but if he is still around or waiting to be brought back from torpor, that diablerie attempt by Sarrasine might arguably fit Michael's stated criteria of a Kindred who was killed and brought back. That he has a history with Michael makes him all the better as a choice for Michael's third.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T04:38:28-07:00","id":1481447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481384#post1481384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481209#post1481209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, plenty of wars in the late middle ages and renaissance for one to fit a &quot;dark ages equivalent&quot; into. But yeah, Dylan is not a great fit anyway, his whole reason to be cited in the first place is being the recurrent infernalist in BJD's plotline, truth be told. By that logic any other major infernalist NPC might do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wasn't Khayt'all diablerized his childe a scant few decades after the 4th crusade for messing up so badly and weakening their clan's standing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed, that was cited as his canon fate in his footnote in CoBN, but i'm pretty sure later books revised that and mention how he came up with some workarounds to survive Sarrasine's betrayal. <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Khay&#39;tall\" target=\"_blank\">Some bits</a> and possible book sources are cited in his wiki write-up (that seems to posit him as a philosophical forerunner of the Ministry, among other things).<br /> <br /> As an aside, i suspect Khay'tall's return might have been inspired by his appearance in modern times as a VtES card. Not blaming the writer, whoever it is, for that, i also love to pull some random bit from them for plotlines with which to monkeywrench lore or metaplot expectations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> [Speaking of which, check out the many versions of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sarrasine\" target=\"_blank\">Sarrasine</a> in VtES at the end of his write-up. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SBjQ9tuuTJQ\" target=\"_blank\">One of these things is not like the other</a>]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-15-2023, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T08:55:38-07:00","id":1481600,"title":"","content":"So we might be looking at something like Mithras and Monty or Michael and Mari in other words. There should be a warning for weaker generation about the perils of diablerizing potent methusalths when they learn about it.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T11:36:09-07:00","id":1481610,"title":"","content":"Side tangent, but I absolutely love the fact that Saulot's soul's survival of his diablerie isn't unique anymore. It impacts the flavor of the World of Darkness in a way that I like if the immortal soul is beyond the ability of a mere vampire to actually destroy. It affirms that there are greater powers at work than the vampires, without getting outside the game's lane and requiring crossovers to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T13:25:51-07:00","id":1481616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481610#post1481610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side tangent, but I absolutely love the fact that Saulot's soul's survival of his diablerie isn't unique anymore. It impacts the flavor of the World of Darkness in a way that I like if the immortal soul is beyond the ability of a mere vampire to actually destroy. It affirms that there are greater powers at work than the vampires, without getting outside the game's lane and requiring crossovers to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really an attestment of those vampire's power and will, rather than any indication of a greater power. If that was that case, you wouldn't just be able to erase younger kindred's souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T13:35:32-07:00","id":1481617,"title":"","content":"I dunno, do their souls really die? Or are they just buried under the stronger entity who took them in? What gauge would we use to measure that? There's clearly something junking up the diablerist's aura...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T14:33:28-07:00","id":1481618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480768-what-is-michael-doing?p=1481600#post1481600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we might be looking at something like Mithras and Monty or Michael and Mari in other words. There should be a warning for weaker generation about the perils of diablerizing potent methusalths when they learn about it.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Truth be told, i remember toying with such a conceit in the form of weird flashbacks to times before a diablerist embrace, tales of kindred a character knew were gone making short cameos in occasions a PC lost a few hours or nights to frenzy among other things a year or two before DSotBH.<br /> <br /> A friend even had a subplot in a chronicle of his involving a number of highly-placed Tremere elders probably being ridden by the Salubri they supposedly consumed, all of them willing servant-sacrifices watching out for the eventual return of Saulot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-15-2023, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T19:45:51-07:00","id":1481636,"title":"","content":"Funny thing about everyone wanting to create or recreate a Dream is that well... the whole idea to create a perfect society for vampires, which was what occurred supposedly in Constantinople under the Trinity, needs... well, a society. So you can't really make that without people knowing.<br /> The 1st and 2nd City, Carthage, Rome, Constantinople, Vykos plans for the Sabbat, and probably some other examples, were all some form of Dream, and well... they failed. Some got pretty close, but I guess the whole problem of them is that they were openly known. Perhaps this new Dream may work because somehow it is being done in the shadows. Which is very Camarilla like.<br /> <br /> I kept wondering just what the hell is Michael's Dream now, since he was eaten by Mary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}